 lists (https://lists.witness-network.org/mailman3/hyperkitty/list/participate%40lists.witness-network.org/thread/J5ZRRQ2EQRVIFF7LL23TWMTL4AVCLYNZ/)\nciteturn24search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: last week; Crawled: last week; Intended users: MCP clients and security tooling that want to check whether the tool definitions they received are the ones the server serves to everyone (split-view detection for tool definitions), and researchers using the weekly open dataset (doi:10.5281/zenodo.23512759).\nWhat it is: HISTOR is a public, append-only log of the tool definitions that MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers listed in the official MCP registry actually serve. Each observation becomes a signed statement, and the statements are leaves of an RFC 9162 Merkle tree (currently about 1.29 million leaves, growing by a few thousand a day). The format is specified at https://github.com/alexar76/histor/blob/main/docs/spec/transparency-log.md https://github.com/alexar76/histor/blob/main/docs/spec/transparency-log.md with test vectors; the checkpoint and note formats were checked byte for byte against golang.org/x/mod/sumdb/note and github.com/transparency-dev/formats/note. Intended users: MCP clients and security tooling that want to check whether the tool definitions they received are the ones the server serves to everyone (split-view detection for tool definitions), and researchers using the weekly open dataset (doi:10.5281/zenodo.23512759). Witness cosignatures are what would turn the log's own signed heads into evidence that it shows everyone the same tree. Load versus utility: 144 add-checkpoint requests per witness per day, small checkpoints, no burst. Expected lifetime: long-lived; the log has run since September 2026 and the origin and key will not change. The same instance also implements c2sp.org/tlog-witness https://histor.modelmarket.dev/witness/v1, https://histor.modelmarket.dev/witness/v1, key histor.modelmarket.dev/witness+87df9f83+BHmgo3SRWlaehFMgWBDIOWFgs1V2Y